  "gloss": "the noun comes first",
  "title": "Noun first: rumah besar",
  "pattern": "noun + describing word: rumah besar · yang + describing word: yang besar",
  "explanation": "A describing word comes after its noun, the opposite of English: rumah besar is 'a big house', kopi panas 'hot coffee', orang baik 'a good person'. With two, both follow the noun: mobil merah baru, a new red car. Ini and itu come last of all: rumah besar itu, that big house. To pick one out from several, use yang, 'the one that's': yang besar is 'the big one', and Saya mau yang merah is 'I'd like the red one'.",
  "natural": "Yang does a lot of work in shops and warungs, where the noun is obvious: Yang ini, Bu (This one, please), Mau yang pedas atau tidak? (Spicy or not?)",
  "stiff": "Putting the describing word first, as in English, is wrong: besar rumah, panas kopi. And yang isn't needed every time: rumah besar is just 'a big house', while rumah yang besar picks out 'the house that's big', as opposed to the small one.",
